# How to use ws-api

| Package | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `@nu-art/ws-api-shared` | `WsEnvelope`, builtins, encode/parse |
| `@nu-art/ws-api-backend` | `ModuleBE_WsApi` — attach to `HttpServer`, auth, handlers |

## When

Realtime / play after HTTP auth. HTTP stays for auth, signed URLs, bootstrap.

## Do

1. `setAuthenticator` with app session/JWT logic (reject → `false`).
2. `registerHandler(type, handler)` before or after attach.
3. `attach(httpServer)` then `startServer()` (upgrade path default `/ws`).
4. Send/receive JSON envelopes `{ type, id?, payload? }`.

## Don't

- Don't invent a permanent app-only WS stack when this lib exists.
- Don't put rooms/presence in v0 — not implemented yet.
- Don't use socket.io for this Thunderstorm path.
